# Requests now go through EasyTolet.Gateway. Start the gateway and target service first.
# Use an authorized test account. Registration alone does not grant admin permissions.
@baseUrl = https://localhost:7001
@accessToken = REPLACE_WITH_JWT_WITH_admin.roles.manage_PERMISSION
@roleId = 1

### List roles (permission: admin.roles.manage)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/roles?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get role
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/roles/{{roleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Create role (also requires positive numeric user_id claim)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roleCode": "TENANT",
  "roleName": "Tenant",
  "parentRoleId": null,
  "description": "Tenant role",
  "isActive": true
}

### Update role
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/roles/{{roleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roleCode": "TENANT",
  "roleName": "Tenant",
  "parentRoleId": null,
  "description": "Updated tenant role",
  "isActive": true
}

### Soft-delete role (run intentionally against a test role)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/roles/{{roleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
